{"api":"openai-completions","content":[{"thinking":"Let me review my two files against the review notes:\n\n1. 检查计划是否误把瞬时事件当持久状态 (Check if the plan mistakenly treats transient events as persistent state)\n2. 是否遗漏重启恢复和幂等取消 (Whether restart recovery and idempotent cancellation are missing)\n3. 风险清单必须为每个高风险项给出验证方式 (Risk checklist must give verification methods for each high-risk item)\n\nLet me re-read my files and check for issues.\n\nImplementation plan:\n- B2 进度事件通道 - \"仅供 UI 展示，无持久化路径\" - good\n- B1 - \"结束时只把最终事实写入 Product Owner\" - good\n- A2 取消幂等 - covered\n- D1 启动恢复 - covered\n- 依赖关系图 - let me check: A1 ──> A2 ──> B1 ... wait, does A2 depend on A1? A2 is 取消幂等语义. Actually the dependency graph says A1 ──> A2, but A2 (cancellation idempotency semantics) doesn't really depend on A1 (database). Actually the table says \"A1、A2 无前置依赖，可并行\" but the dependency graph shows A1 ──> A2. That's a contradiction!\n\nLet me check the implementation plan:\n\n```\nA1 ──> A2 ──> B1 ──> C1 ──> C2\n  \\        \\      └─> D1 ──> D2\n   └────────┘\n```\n\nThe graph shows A1 → A2 (A2 depends on A1), but the text says \"A1、A2 无前置依赖，可并行。\" That's a contradiction. Also \"B1、B2 依赖 A1（A2 的幂等语义为 B1 的取消提供前提，实际依赖 A1+A2）\" - hmm, this says B1 depends on A1, and actually depends on A1+A2. But the graph shows A2 ──> B1, meaning B1 depends on A2. The graph lines: \"A1 ──> A2 ──> B1\" so B1 depends on A2 which depends on A1. But text says \"B1、B2 依赖 A1\" — B1 depends on A1 only per text, but the graph says B1 depends on A2. There's ambiguity.\n\nActually wait, the graph line 2: \"\\        \\      └─> D1 ──> D2\" - the └─> from A1... no wait. Let me parse:\n\n```\nA1 ──> A2 ──> B1 ──> C1 ──> C2\n  \\        \\      └─> D1 ──> D2\n   └────────┘\n```\n\n- Row 1: A1 → A2 → B1 → C1 → C2\n- Row 2: the \"\\\" under A1 goes to \"└─> D1\" (A1 → D1), the \"\\\" under A2 goes to \"└─> D1\"? Hmm, \"\\        \\      └─> D1\" — the second \\ is under A2, pointing down to the └─> D1. So A2 → D1 too? And \"└────────┘\" connects back... This is confusing ASCII art.\n\nThe text below says:\n- A1、A2 无前置依赖，可并行。\n- B1、B2 依赖 A1（A2 的幂等语义为 B1 的取消提供前提，实际依赖 A1+A2）。\n- C1 依赖 B1、B2；C2 依赖 C1。\n- D1 依赖 A1、B1；D2 为最终联调。\n\nSo text says A1 and A2 have no prerequisites and can be parallel. But the graph shows A1 → A2. Contradiction. Also, D1 depends on A1, B1 — but B1 depends on A2 (for cancellation), so D1 transitively depends on A2. The graph's A2 → D1 line might indicate that, but it's ambiguous.\n\nThis is a genuine contradiction I should fix: either A2 depends on A1 or they're parallel. A2 (状态机与取消幂等语义) doesn't need the database; it's a state machine definition. A1 (数据库表与仓储) stores the state. They're largely independent — the state machine could be defined first, or the DB first. Making them parallel is cleaner. So I should fix the graph to show A1 and A2 parallel, both feeding B1 and D1.\n\nLet me also check other potential issues:\n\n1. \"误把瞬时事件当持久状态\" — the plan explicitly says B2 events are transient only. But is there any place where the plan lets events become state? In C2 UI: \"进度展示（订阅 Runtime Event 刷新）\" — that's fine, UI subscribes for display only. In B1: \"周期性把瞬时进度通过 Runtime Event 发出；结束时只把最终事实写入 Product Owner\" — good.\n\nBut wait — one subtle issue: in A1, the table includes \"完成行数\" (completed rows) which could be seen as transient progress being persisted. Hmm. The table has 总行数、完成行数、错误信息、最终结果. Is 完成行数 a transient progress value persisted? The constraint says Runtime Event must not become final business state, and DB saves final task facts. Persisting 完成行数 in the DB is a \"final task fact\" (e.g., total rows completed at end), which is fine as long as during execution, progress is only via events and the DB is only updated at completion... Actually, if the DB stores 完成行数 updated during execution, that would blur the boundary. The review note asks: \"检查计划是否误把瞬时事件当持久状态\". My A1 mentions the table with 完成行数 but doesn't specify when it's written. To be safe, I could clarify that the DB row is written at final state transitions (creation + final update), and 完成行数 is the final count persisted at completion — progress during execution flows only via Runtime Event. Let me add a clarification to A1: 表字段仅记录最终事实；执行期间进度不写库，仅在任务到达终态时一次性写入完成行数等最终数据。\n\nActually, hmm. Is that over-engineering? The review note explicitly says to check this. Adding a clarifying sentence strengthens it. Let me add: \"执行期间不得将瞬时进度写入该表；进度仅经 Runtime Event 传递，任务到达终态时一次性写入最终完成行数。\"\n\n2. \"是否遗漏重启恢复和幂等取消\" — I have D1 启动恢复 and A2 取消幂等. Both covered. But let me double check D1 covers \"重启后继续查看最终结果\" — D1 says \"应用启动时由 Product Owner 读取未完成/已完成任务，恢复中断的 running 任务或将其标记为 failed\". And C2 says \"重启后的结果展示\". D2 end-to-end covers \"发起 → 进度 → 取消 → 重启 → 查看结果\". OK covered.\n\n3. \"风险清单必须为每个高风险项给出验证方式\" — all 10 risks have 验证方式 columns. Good.\n\nAdditional issues to check for contradiction:\n\n- In implementation plan, B1 验证 says \"取消信号能中断执行\" and B2 验证 says \"测试确认事件不含且不更新任何最终业务状态字段\". Good.\n\n- The dependency graph contradicts the text. Fix the graph.\n\n- A1 says \"验证：单测覆盖状态迁移与持久化读写\" — state machine is A2's concern (A2 defines 取消幂等 and states). A1 covering 状态迁移 overlaps with A2. Not necessarily a contradiction, but A1 covers DB + state machine transitions... Actually A1 says \"状态机：pending → running → succeeded | failed | canceled\" and A2 says \"定义 cancel 处理规则\". There's overlap: A1 defines the state machine, A2 defines cancel semantics. Fine, but the validation duplication (\"状态迁移\" test in both A1 and A2? A1's 验证 says \"单测覆盖状态迁移与持久化读写\", A2's 验证 says \"单测覆盖...三种场景\" which includes 并发重复取消. The 状态迁移 in A1 could be interpreted as full state machine testing which belongs to A2. Minor overlap, not critical. I could adjust A1's validation to \"持久化读写与表结构\" and leave 状态迁移 tests to A2. That removes overlap. Let me refine: A1 验证：单测覆盖表结构与持久化读写（含重启后数据仍在）。A2 验证：状态机迁移 + 取消幂等三场景。That's cleaner.\n\n- Risk checklist: \"取消后任务仍在后台写库（竞态）\" — mitigation mentions 原子状态迁移. Good, has verification.\n\n- Risk #9 \"任务结果超过存储限制或含敏感数据\" — is that a high-risk item? It has verification anyway. Fine.\n\n- One more check on constraints: \"验证不包含打包\" — D2 says \"本阶段不涉及打包验证\" and risk #10 mentions 验收不包含打包. Good.\n\n- \"本次不实现云同步\" — risk #10 mentions no cloud sync. Good.\n\nNow let me also re-verify the \"B1、B2 依赖 A1（A2 的幂等语义为 B1 的取消提供前提，实际依赖 A1+A2）\" text vs graph. The graph shows A2 → B1 (via A1 → A2 → B1). Text says B1 depends on A1+A2. So after fixing the graph to parallel A1/A2, B1 should depend on A1+A2, and the graph should show both A1 and A2 feeding B1.\n\nD1 依赖 A1、B1 — but D1 is 启动恢复 which needs cancellation idempotency? Recovery reads DB (A1) and re-schedules (B1). B1 transitively includes A2. Fine as stated.\n\nLet me redraw the graph:\n\n```\nA1 ──┐\n     ├──> B1 ──> C1 ──> C2\nA2 ──┘      │\n     └──> D1 ──> D2\n```\n\nHmm, D1 depends on A1 and B1. So:\n\n```\nA1 ──┬──> B1 ──> C1 ──> C2\nA2 ──┘   │\n         └──> D1 ──> D2\n```\n\nWait, D1 also depends on A1 directly (reads DB at startup). B1 → D1 covers A1 transitively since B1 depends on A1. But A2? D1 recovery doesn't need A2's idempotent cancel per se, but B1 already includes it. Let me write:\n\n```\nA1 ──┬──> B1 ──> C1 ──> C2\nA2 ──┘   │\n         └──> D1 ──> D2\n```\n\nAnd the bullet list:\n- A1、A2 无前置依赖，可并行。\n- B1 依赖 A1（执行器需要数据库）与 A2（取消依赖幂等语义）；B2 依赖 A1（事件结构本身不依赖，但事件与执行器联调需要 A1）— hmm, does B2 actually depend on A1? B2 is the event channel structure; it doesn't need the DB. The text said \"B1、B2 依赖 A1\". B2 arguably doesn't depend on A1 at all — it's just an event definition. But it pairs with B1 for integration tests. To keep it simple: B1 依赖 A1+A2；B2 无前置依赖（仅事件结构定义），与 B1 联调时依赖 B1。Hmm, but that changes the plan structure. Is this worth it? The review note doesn't specifically ask about B2's dependency. The current text \"B1、B2 依赖 A1（A2 的幂等语义为 B1 的取消提供前提，实际依赖 A1+A2）\" is a bit muddled — it says B1、B2 depend on A1, then clarifies B1 actually depends on A1+A2. It doesn't clarify B2's actual dependency. B2 (event channel) truly doesn't need the DB. Let me make it precise: \"B1 依赖 A1（执行落库）与 A2（取消幂等）；B2 仅定义事件结构，无数据依赖，但其集成验证依赖 B1（事件由执行器发出）\".\n\nActually let me be careful not to over-engineer the revision. The review notes ask three specific things:\n1. 计划是否误把瞬时事件当持久状态 → add explicit clarification in A1/A2/B2 about progress not persisted; also check the D1 \"恢复中断的 running 任务\" — recovery implies the DB knows a task was running, which is a final fact (status=running persisted at start? or derived?). Hmm. When a task starts, is \"running\" persisted? If yes, that's a final fact (task fact: it was started), and progress is separate. That's consistent: DB holds task facts (including current phase status like running), Runtime Event holds instantaneous progress (percent). The constraint says \"Runtime Event 只传递瞬时进度，数据库保存最终任务事实\" — so DB may hold status transitions; percent/progress stays in events. My A1 table includes 完成行数 — I'll clarify it's written only at terminal state. Good.\n\n2. 是否遗漏重启恢复和幂等取消 → both present; confirm in reply.\n\n3. 风险清单每个高风险项有验证方式 → all rows have 验证方式; confirm.\n\nPlus the graph/text contradiction (A1 → A2 vs 可并行) — genuine bug to fix.\n\nAlso A1/A2 validation overlap — minor, fix.\n\nLet me also double-check the risk checklist for \"每个高风险项给出验证方式\" — every row has a 验证方式 cell. Good.\n\nOne more: in implementation plan C2 UI \"验证：手工/UI 测试覆盖发起、进度更新、取消、重启后查看结果\" — includes restart viewing. Good.\n\nAlso check: does the plan anywhere treat Runtime Event as persistent? B2: \"仅供 UI 展示，无持久化路径\" — good. Risk #1 covers it. \n\nNow let me make the edits.\n\nEdit 1 (implementation-plan.md): A1 说明 — add explicit \"执行期间进度不写库，仅到达终态时一次性写入最终完成行数等最终事实\".\n\nCurrent A1 text:\n```\n- **A1. 数据库表与仓储**\n  - 说明：新增 `import_tasks` 表（id、类型、状态、总行数、完成行数、错误信息、最终结果、创建/更新时间）。状态机：`pending → running → succeeded | failed | canceled`。\n  - 职责归属：Product Owner + 数据库。\n  - 验证：单测覆盖状态迁移与持久化读写；重启后数据仍在。\n```\n\nNew:\n```\n- **A1. 数据库表与仓储**\n  - 说明：新增 `import_tasks` 表（id、类型、状态、总行数、完成行数、错误信息、最终结果、创建/更新时间）。状态机：`pending → running → succeeded | failed | canceled`。该表只保存任务最终事实：执行期间的瞬时进度（百分比、当前行数）一律不写库，仅经 Runtime Event 传递；完成行数等数值只在任务到达终态时一次性写入。\n  - 职责归属：Product Owner + 数据库。\n  - 验证：单测覆盖表结构与持久化读写（含重启后数据仍在）；确认执行期间无进度写库路径。\n```\n\nEdit 2: A2 验证 refine:\nCurrent: `- 验证：单测覆盖“取消已终态任务”“取消运行中任务”“并发重复取消”三种场景。`\nThat's fine actually. And A1's 状态迁移 test moved to... hmm, if I remove 状态迁移 from A1's validation, where does it go? A2 covers cancel scenarios; state machine transitions (pending→running→succeeded etc.) should be tested somewhere. A2 is \"任务状态机与取消幂等语义\" — its name includes 状态机. So A2 验证 could include 状态机迁移. Let me update A2 验证: `单测覆盖状态机全量迁移与“取消已终态任务”“取消运行中任务”“并发重复取消”三种场景。`\n\nEdit 3: Fix dependency graph and bullets.\n\nCurrent:\n```\n## 依赖关系图\n\n```\nA1 ──> A2 ──> B1 ──> C1 ──> C2\n  \\        \\      └─> D1 ──> D2\n   └────────┘\n```\n\n- A1、A2 无前置依赖，可并行。\n- B1、B2 依赖 A1（A2 的幂等语义为 B1 的取消提供前提，实际依赖 A1+A2）。\n- C1 依赖 B1、B2；C2 依赖 C1。\n- D1 依赖 A1、B1；D2 为最终联调。\n```\n\nNew:\n```\n## 依赖关系图\n\n```\nA1 ──┬──> B1 ──> C1 ──> C2\nA2 ──┘   │\n         └──> D1 ──> D2\n```\n\n- A1、A2 无前置依赖，可并行。\n- B1 依赖 A1（执行落库）与 A2（取消依赖幂等语义）；B2 仅定义事件结构、无数据依赖，但事件由执行器发出，其集成验证依赖 B1。\n- C1 依赖 B1、B2；C2 依赖 C1。\n- D1 依赖 A1（读取任务事实）与 B1（恢复调度）；D2 为最终联调。\n```\n\nHmm wait, the graph: A1 ──┬──> B1 and A2 ──┘ — that shows both A1 and A2 feeding B1. And \"└──> D1\" from B1. D1 also depends on A1 directly, but transitively through B1. The bullet says D1 依赖 A1 与 B1. The graph shows D1 depends on B1 only. To be more accurate, I could show A1 also feeding D1:\n\n```\nA1 ──┬──> B1 ──> C1 ──> C2\nA2 ──┘   │\n         ├──> D1 ──> D2\nA1 ──────┘\n```\n\nThat's getting messy. Simpler: keep it clear that D1 depends on B1 (which transitively includes A1) and note direct A1 dependency in bullets. Or:\n\n```\nA1 ──┬──> B1 ──> C1 ──> C2\nA2 ──┘   │\nA1 ──────┴──> D1 ──> D2\n```\n\nHmm. Let me just do:\n\n```\nA1 ──┬──> B1 ──> C1 ──> C2\nA2 ──┘   │\n         └──> D1 ──> D2\n```\n\nwith bullets clarifying D1 依赖 A1、B1（图中经 B1 传递，A1 为直接依赖）。Actually simpler to write bullets and keep graph minimal. I'll write:\n\n- D1 依赖 A1（直接读取）与 B1（恢复调度，经 B1 亦传递 A1/A2 依赖）；D2 为最终联调。\n\nOK. Let me now also consider whether to keep \"A2 ──> B1\" — yes, B1 needs A2's idempotent cancel.\n\nNow let me write the edits with edit_file.\n\nAlso risk checklist — check for any omissions vs review notes. All items have verification. I think risk list is fine. Maybe add one risk about \"重启恢复策略\" already covered (#8). Fine.\n\nLet me apply edits to implementation-plan.md.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content","type":"thinking"},{"text":"已读取 `project/review-notes.md`。复审要点：①瞬时事件不得被当持久状态；②不得遗漏重启恢复与幂等取消；③风险清单每个高风险项必须有验证方式。\n\n对照检查后发现以下问题，直接修订原文件：","type":"text"},{"arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"- **A1. 数据库表与仓储**\n  - 说明：新增 `import_tasks` 表（id、类型、状态、总行数、完成行数、错误信息、最终结果、创建/更新时间）。状态机：`pending → running → succeeded | failed | canceled`。该表只保存任务最终事实：执行期间的瞬时进度（百分比、当前行数等）一律不写库，仅经 Runtime Event 传递；完成行数等数值只在任务到达终态时一次性写入。\n  - 职责归属：Product Owner + 数据库。\n  - 验证：单测覆盖表结构与持久化读写（含重启后数据仍在）；确认执行期间无进度写库路径。","oldText":"- **A1. 数据库表与仓储**\n  - 说明：新增 `import_tasks` 表（id、类型、状态、总行数、完成行数、错误信息、最终结果、创建/更新时间）。状态机：`pending → running → succeeded | failed | canceled`。\n  - 职责归属：Product Owner + 数据库。\n  - 验证：单测覆盖状态迁移与持久化读写；重启后数据仍在。"},{"newText":"  - 验证：单测覆盖状态机全量迁移（pending → running → succeeded | failed | canceled），以及“取消已终态任务”“取消运行中任务”“并发重复取消”三种场景。","oldText":"  - 验证：单测覆盖“取消已终态任务”“取消运行中任务”“并发重复取消”三种场景。"},{"newText":"```\nA1 ──┬──> B1 ──> C1 ──> C2\nA2 ──┘   │\n         └──> D1 ──> D2\n```\n\n- A1、A2 无前置依赖，可并行。\n- B1 依赖 A1（执行落库）与 A2（取消依赖幂等语义）；B2 仅定义事件结构、无数据依赖，但事件由执行器发出，其集成验证依赖 B1。\n- C1 依赖 B1、B2；C2 依赖 C1。\n- D1 依赖 A1（直接读取任务事实）与 B1（恢复调度，经 B1 传递 A1/A2 依赖）；D2 为最终联调。","oldText":"```\nA1 ──> A2 ──> B1 ──> C1 ──> C2\n  \\        \\      └─> D1 ──> D2\n   └────────┘\n```\n\n- A1、A2 无前置依赖，可并行。\n- B1、B2 依赖 A1（A2 的幂等语义为 B1 的取消提供前提，实际依赖 A1+A2）。\n- C1 依赖 B1、B2；C2 依赖 C1。\n- D1 依赖 A1、B1；D2 为最终联调。"}],"path":"delivery/implementation-plan.md"},"id":"call_00_DMNkkpTSLEdARJ3IEIrz3345","name":"edit_file","type":"toolCall"}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","provider":"deepseek","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","responseId":"de0af53e-fb6d-47e2-9df6-2215f17fee1e","role":"assistant","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788269326258,"usage":{"cacheRead":6272,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":{"cacheRead":0.000017561599999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"input":0.00001904,"output":0.0014756,"total":0.0015122016},"input":136,"output":5270,"reasoning":4455,"totalTokens":11678}}